    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1946637352602067183",
      "url": "https://x.com/CTalisayon/status/1946637352602067183",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/CTalisayon/status/1946637352602067183",
      "text": "In the Philippines, there is one great businessman I look up to. His name is Ramon S. Ang. He is the owner of San Miguel and also a fan of automotive.\n\nI call him Sir Ang.\n\nOne time, I called his office. He wasn’t there, so I only got to speak with his staff. I told them I just needed five minutes of his time—I had a few questions. He had a very busy schedule at that time, so the secretary said she would confirm the schedule. I took it as a decline.\n\nA few hours later, I decided to go out and headed to the grocery store. That’s when I noticed Sir Ang had already sent his men to inspect every drainage I would pass by—just to make sure there would be no flooding in my area.\n\nThat’s a true story, just in case you’re wondering.\n\nI just remembered it today, when I opened my computer and read a few lines from an author I adore. Great men always have a way to hold you—even from a distance.",
